{"schema":"mao-cross-channel-public-site-data/1","script":"0319","rows":[{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0319:00000039:text","row":40861,"ordinal":1,"kind":"text","jp":"「…………」","en":"“…………”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:905528","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccd0022b:00001","en":"Taichi: \"......\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0319:0000005d:text","row":40862,"ordinal":2,"kind":"text","jp":"言いたいことは山ほどあった。","en":"There was so much I wanted to say.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:905529","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccd0022b:00002","en":"The size of the amount of things I wanted to tell were a mountain,","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["grammar","idiom_calque"],"assessment":"The Japanese idiom says he had a mountain of things to say. The English is grammatically malformed and literalizes the quantity twice.","remedy":"There was a mountain of things I wanted to say,","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":66,"start":0,"text":"The size of the amount of things I wanted to tell were a mountain,"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0319:00000091:text","row":40863,"ordinal":3,"kind":"text","jp":"けど、彼女に何を言っても意味はない。","en":"But nothing I could say to her would matter.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:905530","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccd0022b:00003","en":"but whatever I say to her it will have no meaning.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0319:000000cd:text","row":40864,"ordinal":4,"kind":"text","jp":"俺はただ、するべきことをするだけだ。","en":"I would simply do what had to be done.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:905531","unitId":"ghs-tl:ccd0022b:00004","en":"I will simply do what I ought to do, and nothing more.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0319:000001da:text","row":40865,"ordinal":5,"kind":"text","jp":"……………………。","en":"…………………….","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:905532","unitId":"ghs-t